3. STATEMENT OF TERMS (read this before quoting any figure)
==========================================================================

3.1  "1 GSPS" means DIGITAL THROUGHPUT.
     Four lanes at 250 MHz, four complex samples per clock, no dropped samples,
     no back-pressure. It is NOT a sampling rate. There is no 1 GSPS ADC on the
     board; the stimulus is a 2048 x 96-bit on-chip ROM replay. Any sentence of
     the form "1 GSPS sampling rate" is wrong.

3.2  Bandwidth is a MEASURABLE BOUNDARY, not a ceiling.
     The measured -3 dB figure is 768.55 MHz (board measurement, 6296 bins x
     122.07 kHz). The measurable boundary is quoted as 0.80-0.86 GHz, and the
     criterion is whether the fixed-point model and the RTL still agree bin by
     bin - not what the device could theoretically clock at. Do not paraphrase
     this as "maximum bandwidth" or "bandwidth limit reached".

3.3  Simulation is not measurement.
     Behavioural simulation results are labelled L3 (see docs/metrics.md).
     Only board captures are labelled L4. No post-synthesis and no
     post-implementation timing simulation was performed; this is a stated
     limitation, not an omission.

3.4  The chain is open in the analogue domain.
     No analogue front end, no high-speed ADC, no system-level closed loop.
     The design analyses a digital baseband IQ stream that it replays from ROM.


